  <h2>Best Practices</h2>

  <h3>1. Keep Expressions Simple</h3>
  <p>
    Break complex expressions into multiple lines or use intermediate variables.
    This improves readability and debugging.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Use Meaningful Names</h3>
  <p>
    Entity and attribute names should be self-documenting. Avoid abbreviations
    unless they're universally understood.
  </p>

  <h3>3. Handle Edge Cases</h3>
  <p>
    Check for null values and empty arrays before operations. Use default values
    where appropriate.
  </p>

  <h3>4. Avoid Side Effects in Conditions</h3>
  <p>
    Conditions should be pure boolean expressions. Save modifications for actions.
  </p>

